_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"46d362d64a23e82f44d44306971dfb86d56d400347953283ed56128562db8895","event_uuid":"d874f305-a822-4bc5-80b0-21114078db94","position":{"commit_sha":"5ea7cb85614e28e6365bbccde9de2fbce646f467","position":"1794454918632488879-d874f305-a822-4bc5-80b0-21114078db94"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Proposed repair (production write, NOT performed; awaiting operator approval). Run on the host via SSM against the live MCP container; every step is guarded and stops on the first failure:\n\n```\nC=$(docker ps --format '{{.Names}}' | grep '^rebar-mcp' | head -1)\ndocker exec \"$C\" sh -c 'cd \"$MCP_CODE_DIR\" &&\n  git diff --cached --quiet e2ed08b343a2be462de4433a93edbb5cbc062a52 &&\n  git diff --quiet &&\n  test -z \"$(git ls-files --others --exclude-standard)\" &&\n  git update-ref -m \"repair interrupted fast-forward\" HEAD e2ed08b343a2be462de4433a93edbb5cbc062a52 3835269d792b7764e0beeca95798250487c78895 &&\n  test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\" &&\n  git fetch origin main && git merge --ff-only origin/main &&\n  git rev-list --left-right --count HEAD...origin/main'\n```\n\nWhy this is safe: the first 3 checks prove the index and working tree already ARE e2ed08b343a and nothing else; update-ref is compare-and-swap against the current HEAD, so it only moves the branch onto the tree already on disk (no file is rewritten, nothing is discarded). After that the tree is clean and the runbook's own break-glass fast-forward (review-bot-ops.md \"MCP code workspace freshness\") applies. Expected final line `0 0`. Then re-run the read-only in-container resolution: frontier/standard/trivial should read opus-5-5 / sonnet-5-5 / haiku-5-5. load_config re-stats rebar.toml on each call, so no restart is expected to be needed; that is unverified until the resolution check runs.","timestamp":1794363688699780194},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Refinement 2026-11-10 18:45 PST: which model runs depends on the gate path, not only on the workspace.\n- Async MCP gate starters (review_plan_start, verify_completion_start) materialize an attested snapshot at current origin/main: both REVIEW_RESULTs recorded verified_at_sha 91182f96362 and ran_model bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5 (verifier), and CloudWatch shows us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5 Invocations during those runs (18:20 PST bucket: 269). Those paths ARE on 5.5.\n- The completion gate inside transition_ticket(closed) on itchy-neutral-whooper recorded verified_at_sha 3835269d792 (the stuck workspace HEAD) and model bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6; CloudWatch shows sonnet-4-6 Invocations (3) in the same 18:25 PST bucket. So the close gate still runs on the stuck workspace's code and 4.x config, and signs a verdict against a 13-day-old tree.\nSo the impact is: every completion-gated close over production MCP verifies against 3835269d792 with 4.x models. The repair in the previous comment fixes both; whether the close path should resolve origin/main like the starters do is a separate question for this bug's root-cause criterion.","timestamp":1794364256598124821},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-10 19:00 PST: OPEN, unclaimed (hold on new bugs). Evidence and the guarded repair command are in the comments above. The repair is a production write and waits for operator approval. After repair: run the read-only in-container model resolution and confirm `0 0` against origin/main. Root cause of the interrupted fast-forward is not identified: the rebar-mcp journal has nothing for 2026-10-28 17:30-18:10 PDT.","timestamp":1794365988387469277},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"New symptom 2026-11-10 22:16 PST (session 3d705fec): MCP claim_ticket on volcanic-prim-parakeet refused with \"the code the plan was reviewed against drifted: 4 dependency file(s) changed (docs/jira-sync-setup.md, src/rebar/reconciler/mutation_payloads.py, tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_mutation_payloads.py, tests/unit/reconciler/test_field_contract_properties.py)\". Those are exactly the files change 3345 (ed6ba4c4e9b, merged ~21:13 PST) touched. The same certificate checks `certified` at verified_at_sha ed6ba4c4e9b with the worktree CLI (`rebar review-plan --status`), and the worktree CLI claim succeeded. Consistent with the MCP server evaluating claim-gate currency against its lagging code workspace; not independently confirmed on the host (production read-only, not inspected this session).","timestamp":1794377868572080134},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Workspace repaired 2026-11-11 (PST), operator-authorized production write, via SSM AWS-RunShellScript on i-00880b2c7f13527c5 (command 86220c94-547d-449d-8164-b73dc2d0f02f).\n\nSequence: the 3 guards passed (staged tree == e2ed08b343a, no unstaged edits, no untracked files); `git update-ref HEAD e2ed08b343a <old 3835269d792>`; tree clean; `git fetch origin main && git merge --ff-only origin/main`.\n\nVerified after (separate read-only SSM check):\n- live container is now rebar-mcp-b878c4be7686-8093; MCP_CODE_DIR HEAD b878c4be768, `HEAD...origin/main` = `0 0`, `git status --porcelain` empty\n- rebar.toml: default bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5; frontier opus-5-5, standard sonnet-5-5, trivial haiku-5-5\n- `LLMConfig.from_env()` in the container resolves default = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5\n\nStill open on this bug: the root cause in code — the entrypoint silently refuses to refresh a dirty workspace (logged `dirty code checkout — refusing to refresh` on every start since 2026-10-29 with no alert). Not yet verified: a close-path completion check now verifies against current main rather than 3835269d792.","timestamp":1794423435923707325},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause (read-only journal evidence, host i-00880b2c7f13527c5). Times are 2026-10-29 UTC; PDT is 7 hours earlier.\n- 00:40:19 and 00:46:19: rebar-health logs container rebar-mcp-e2ed08b343a2-8092 at memory_rss 3.31 GB and 3.37 GB.\n- 00:47:26: kernel `Memory cgroup out of memory: Killed process 1648385 (rebar-mcp)`. The cgroup is the container's docker scope (limit 3801088 kB). dockerd records the task delete at 00:47:27.\n- 00:47:28: the workspace index was written (its mtime). HEAD stayed at 3835269d792 while the index and working tree became e2ed08b343a, the commit that container was deployed for.\nThe container's background refresh (`git merge --ff-only origin/main` inside refresh_code_locked) was killed between writing the checkout and moving the ref, during an OOM of the same container. Every later start then saw a \"dirty\" tree and refused, with only a stderr line.\nFix in progress: (1) the entrypoint recovers exactly that provable state: index tree == a commit on HEAD..origin/main, no unstaged or untracked change, compare-and-swap ref move. Otherwise it refuses and emits an `MCP_CODE_WORKSPACE_ERROR {...}` marker. (2) The autodeploy steady-state tick checks the live backend's workspace and emits AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-code-workspace-stuck, which the existing rebar-autodeploy-errors alarm pages on. No config key, env var or Terraform change.","timestamp":1794424730523381767},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fix landed and verified, 2026-11-11 19:29 PST.\n- Change 3355 merged as d583578c4da (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved; make verify rc=0: 21,019 + 218 passed). It has 2 parts. (1) mcp-entrypoint.sh recovers the interrupted fast-forward: index tree == a commit on HEAD..origin/main, nothing unstaged or untracked, compare-and-swap ref move, against the last fetched main even when the remote is unreachable. Otherwise it refuses with an MCP_CODE_WORKSPACE_ERROR marker. (2) The autodeploy steady-state tick probes the live backend's workspace and emits AUTODEPLOY_ERROR mcp-code-workspace-stuck when it is dirty, unreadable, exec-failed, or its HEAD lacks the live image's commit; the existing rebar-autodeploy-errors alarm pages on that. Tests reproduce the stuck state with a real repo (tests/infra/test_mcp_entrypoint.py) and run the real probe script (tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py); negative controls confirmed the recovery, the unstaged guard and the behind check each fail their test when removed. No config key, env var or flag.\n- Production after deploy (read-only SSM): mcp-deployed-sha d583578c4da; live container rebar-mcp-d583578c4da3-8093; MCP_CODE_DIR HEAD d583578c4da == main, 0 porcelain entries; the deployed entrypoint contains the recovery; 0 mcp-code-workspace-stuck markers in the last 10 min.\n- Close-path check: before the repair, a close verified at 3835269d792 with sonnet-4-6 (itchy-neutral-whooper). After the repair, the MCP close of 2473-79b7-1048-4a71 at 16:52 PST verified at fdf0a94aba8, which was main's tip at that moment (committed 16:44 PST), with ran_model bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5. This bug's own close below is a further data point.\n- Root cause recorded above: an OOM kill of rebar-mcp-e2ed08b343a2-8092 at 2026-10-28 17:47:26 PDT, mid-refresh.\n- Residual, filed separately (not this bug): juiced-anarthrous-bird. The workspace refreshes only at container start, so between MCP-path deploys a close verifies against the last MCP deploy's commit, not main.","timestamp":1794454211408431309},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 ~19:50 PST: CLOSED (class regression, completion signature signed). Fix 3355 merged as d583578c4da and deployed (live rebar-mcp-d583578c4da3-8093, workspace clean at main). This close's own completion verdict verified against d583578c4da == origin/main with ran_model bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5, which is the close-path confirmation. The first close attempt failed only because criterion 1 lacked the [non-codebase] tag; the tag was added, the plan re-reviewed (PASS, certified), and the close passed. Residual lag between MCP deploys is filed as juiced-anarthrous-bird.","timestamp":1794454918632488879}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794362726608311101,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ae855f8a-eb44-4e85-a2ff-5209c233c526","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2918-dbd3-9379-4d09"},{"link_uuid":"d7b8c1fa-4836-4137-bbc3-30bdd5d7c784","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1ac8-a2c4-7d4c-4e23"}],"description":"## Observed (read-only over SSM, 2026-11-10 ~17:35 PST, host i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\n\n- Live MCP container `rebar-mcp-06b3b1a52303-8093` (image built at 06b3b1a5230, up ~23 h, healthy). Its env sets `REBAR_ROOT=MCP_CODE_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`, so the server reads `rebar.toml` from that workspace, not from the image's `/app`.\n- Workspace HEAD = `3835269d792` (2026-10-28 13:48 PDT). Its `origin/main` was fetched to `06b3b1a5230`; GitHub main is now `91182f96362`.\n- Running `LLMConfig.from_env()` + `resolve_model_string` inside the container resolves: default model `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`; `frontier` → opus-4-8, `standard` → sonnet-4-6, `trivial` → haiku-4-5. main's `rebar.toml` (after 3340 / `06b3b1a5230`) names the 5.5 models. **Production plan review is not running on the 5.5 models.**\n- `git status --porcelain` shows 27 staged entries. The index equals the tree of `e2ed08b343a` exactly (`git diff --cached --quiet e2ed08b343a` → 0), the working tree equals the index, there are 0 untracked files, and `e2ed08b343a^` = `3835269d792`. Index mtime 2026-10-28 17:47:28 PDT; last reflog entry is the 14:14 PDT fast-forward to `3835269d792`.\n- The entrypoint's `refresh_code_locked` refuses a dirty tree, so every restart since logs `mcp: dirty code checkout — refusing refresh` (first journal hit 2026-10-29 17:16 PDT). The refusal is stderr-only; nothing alerted.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n\nThe state matches a fast-forward to `e2ed08b343a` that wrote index and working tree but never moved HEAD (process killed between the two). The killer is unidentified: the rebar-mcp journal has no entries in that window; autodeploy ran its 2-minute MCP reconcile throughout.\n\n## Impact\n\nEvery production gate that resolves config through this workspace uses the pre-3340 config: 4.x models, and any config key added after 2026-10-28. The 5.5 upgrade (and the Opus 5.5 refusal fix verification) is not live.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] [non-codebase] The production workspace is repaired by an operator-approved write and reports `0 0` against origin/main (runbook review-bot-ops.md \"MCP code workspace freshness\"); a fresh in-container resolution shows frontier/standard/trivial on the 5.5 ids.\n  provenance: environment=production rebar host i-00880b2c7f13527c5 (MCP container); principal=frontier operator role via SSM; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — repair by SSM command 86220c94 then read-only in-container git rev-list and LLMConfig resolution, recorded in ticket comments\n- [x] The interrupted-fast-forward state (clean against a descendant commit of HEAD that is an ancestor of origin/main) is either recovered safely by the entrypoint or surfaced loudly (alarm/health), with a test reproducing the stuck state.\n- [x] Root cause of the interruption identified or the evidence searched recorded.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag in the fix.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh","reason":"recover interrupted fast-forward; refusal markers"},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"steady-state stuck-workspace alert"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"runbook"},{"path":"tests/infra/test_mcp_entrypoint.py","reason":"reproduce stuck state"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py","reason":"alert test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","1ac8-a2c4-7d4c-4e23"],["relates_to","2918-dbd3-9379-4d09"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"7b1ce96f-e0d8-4a6b-91e9-d82839ed8ca0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6b02-067c-9dbb-47e7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Production MCP code workspace stuck at 3835269d792 after an interrupted fast-forward, so plan review still resolves 4.x models","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d3d44539-074e-4d21-9ef3-42de649652bb","65ee5839-e646-4e31-aba6-cb4784689c20","e165bc10-4bb6-4033-939f-0b34a668ecc8","7a9dfa8b-0b42-4d71-9475-16633dc62bb5","a8bdd37b-ad17-47dc-91de-116c5a247752","b54bac5c-46d6-410c-8ba7-1ffae8c9c5f8","ae855f8a-eb44-4e85-a2ff-5209c233c526","d7b8c1fa-4836-4137-bbc3-30bdd5d7c784","9f38b4cd-07aa-40f3-8738-5e6af8c0f636","6182df25-7fd4-437e-a4ab-65cc50c1b99f","4adf46f4-6ae2-4118-8a0c-6e69bd9eba5c","75e44464-1711-44ca-a28e-80da32064560","7b1ce96f-e0d8-4a6b-91e9-d82839ed8ca0","62c54051-99b4-40af-9a27-939ac79a3f0a","d874f305-a822-4bc5-80b0-21114078db94"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794454918632488880,"